    {
      "id": "1556569954751352854",
      "type": "Reply",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-05T07:33:16.884+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "Agreed, I think my frame of questioning basically sounds like...\nThicker wheels can more aggressively cut -- BUT these larger wheels chip more. (some of my experience as a machinist)\nThis also means consumables costs go down, machine cost goes down\nBut the cost in silicon goes up (larger saw street) \n\nI'm sure we'll go around and around and they won't give me an answer, I've done this before, but in the end I think they'll guide us towards our optimal solution.",
